  "style": {
    "id": "ripple-interference",
    "name": "Ripple Interference",
    "description": "A shallow ripple tank on a dark walnut bench, seen at a low angle: clear turquoise water over a pale tiled floor, two brass dippers on one brass bar, two corks with small flags floating as markers. The water surface is the exact sum of two travelling ring waves (closed form in t, ripple.js): one water mesh displaced in the vertex shader, normals from the same function per pixel, refraction to the floor with caustic bands, Fresnel reflection of an analytic studio whose low side strip picks out every crest. Corks and dippers evaluate the same function in JS. Sliding one source's timing moves the still lines of calm: the corks swap roles.",
